# Boreal ground cover (with Pine): a WIDE, low dwarf-birch mat - short creeping stems, flat-angled modules spreading
# far sideways, small olive leaf clusters (~0.5-0.9 m tall, ~4-6 m across). It fills the open floor between the pines
# with one piece where the round bushes need three: Weight 2, so half the climate's bushes are one.
